grimoire-linux (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * RTL: stat tile numbers align right like their labels
  * UpdateL: the update summary wraps instead of cutting off the security count
  * SightsL: key chips no longer cut off at the hub's minimum size
  * Settings: Run setup again opens the setup again; hotkey buttons fit long languages
  * AUR: .SRCINFO description matches PKGBUILD
  * PlayL software fallback without QtOpenGL; backups skip ShotL's token; package descriptions
  * prefs.save: a temp file per writer
  * Sign-in: start the session off the UI thread
  * Sign-out failure message: its own string, translated
  * Tray: escape notification text
  * Home cards: show status lines as plain text
  * Accounts, GitHub: a garbled HTTP answer is an error, not a stuck screen
  * Update restart: close the windows before starting the new copy
  * AUR: python-gobject is also what PhoneL and VaultL's show-in-folder service use
  * GitHub backup: one sign-in per profile, not one for the whole PC
  * Restart and sign-out: close the windows first, sign out off the UI thread
  * Self-update waits out the helper prompt; StoreL named with the other root helpers
  * Backups: leave out PlayL's resume points and LaunchL's machine state
  * uninstall.sh --purge: remove Grimoire's sign-ins from the keyring too
  * Hub: read the home cards' status lines off the UI thread
  * Packaging: fix debian/control so the .deb builds again

